NAME: a for in a template leaves the caller's argument alone
DESCRIPTION: the caller passes (ADD 1 i) to a template that repeats it with a (for i ...): the i is the caller's let variable, not the for's numbers (d-7d2612-52b2e3); see behtests/template_for_argument.beh
SRC:
(program
  (define (thrice (c Code)) (for i 1 3 c))
  (let (i 0) (seq (thrice (ADD 1 i)) (JMP 0) (DAT 0 (store i)))))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b

  ADD.AB #1     , $_LET1 
  ADD.AB #1     , $_LET1 
  ADD.AB #1     , $_LET1 
  JMP    #0     , #0     
_LET1 
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  DAT    $0     , $0     